O it's now we're past o' the Lizard lights,
The Start, boys, next will heave in sight ;
We'll soon be abreast of the Isle of Wight ;
O I wonder if my clothes are out o' pawn.
O when we get to the Blackwall docks,
The pretty young girls come down in flocks ;
Some in their petticoats and some in frocks ;
O I wonder if my clothes are out o' pawn.

O fare you well, we're bound away ;
Hurrah! Sing fare you well;
We're bound away this very day,
Hurrah! Sing fare you well.

Fire in the fore-top, fire in the main;
It's fetch a bucket o' water girls, and put it out again.

Fire in the fore-peak, fire down below;
It's fetch a bucket o! water girls, there's fire down below.

Fire in the windlass, fire in the chain;
It's fetch a bucket o? water girls, and put it out again.

Fire up aloft, and fire down below;
It's fetch a bucket o' water girls, there's fire down below.

To Madam Gashees we all will go,
For Madamoiselle you all do know.

O Madamoiselle we'll take her in tow;
We'll take her in tow to Callao

O I wish I was at Madam Gashee's ;
It's there we'll sit and take our ease.

Sally she a "Badian bright Mulatter;
Sally pretty gal, but can't get at her.

Seven long years I courted Sally;
Sally she would flirt but nebber marry.

Nous etions trois marins de Groix,
Embarques sur le Saint Francois ;
Mon traderi, tra la la la,
Mon traderi, tra la la laire.

Embarques sur le Saint Francois,
